From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:41:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: attach a device-specific WLAN DMA pool

IPQ5332 multi-chip firmware needs contiguous buffers inside the Q6
WLAN_SRAM window. A boot argument such as cma=0 can disable the default
CMA pool, leaving QMI unable to allocate shared MLO memory.

Attach a named reserved DMA pool during the common AHB and PCI probe
path. Both radios can allocate from the same pool using their own DMA
device, so existing QMI ownership and address checks apply. Keep the
pool attached through driver teardown. Boards without a named pool
continue to use the normal DMA allocator.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1893,9 +1893,44 @@ enum ath12k_qmi_mem_mode ath12k_core_get
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath12k_core_get_memory_mode);
 
+static void ath12k_core_release_dma_pool(void *data)
+{
+	of_reserved_mem_device_release(data);
+}
+
+static int ath12k_core_init_dma_pool(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+{
+	struct device *dev = ab->dev;
+	struct device_node *pool;
+	bool available;
+	int index, ret;
+
+	index = of_property_match_string(dev->of_node, "memory-region-names",
+					 "wlan-dma");
+	if (index < 0)
+		return 0;
+
+	pool = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "memory-region", index);
+	available = of_device_is_available(pool);
+	of_node_put(pool);
+	if (!available)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "WLAN DMA pool is unavailable\n");
+
+	ret = of_reserved_mem_device_init_by_idx(dev, dev->of_node, index);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to attach WLAN DMA pool\n");
+
+	return devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, ath12k_core_release_dma_pool, dev);
+}
+
 int ath12k_core_pre_init(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	const struct ath12k_mem_profile_based_param *param;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = ath12k_core_init_dma_pool(ab);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	param = &ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[ab->target_mem_mode];
 	/* Long-lived RX ring entries can pin mostly unused shared page fragments.
